WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
- My next guest is a YouTube superstar,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.625
with nearly five million
subscribers so people like him.

00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:07.670
(Manny laughs)

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:12.350
Manny Gutierrez also known
as Manny MUA is a trailblazer

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.910
in the world of cosmetics, y'all.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.650
He's the first male
ambassador for Maybelline,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.040
and his makeup tutorials

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.559
have literally been viewed
nearly 500 million times.

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:23.975
(crowd cheers)

00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:25.900
So he even has a cosmetics brand

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.420
called Lunar Beauty,

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.230
but before Manny was accepted
in the world of cosmetics,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.328
he struggled to be
accepted in his own family.

00:00:32.328 --> 00:00:35.300
Here to share their story
of love and forgiveness

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.130
is Manny Gutierrez and
his father, Manny senior.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.033
Y'all give it up for them.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.920
(crowd cheers)

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.750
So this is my favorite story y'all,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.610
because this happens a lot
in families where people,

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.460
they don't, especially I'm from the south,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.690
and people don't grow up
around the gay culture,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.890
so they're kind of thrown by it,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.588
they don't know how to handle it at first.

00:00:54.588 --> 00:00:55.421
- Absolutely.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:56.460
- And I love y'all so much
for sharing this story.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.310
It's gonna inspire so many people

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.970
but were you always into makeup?

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:00.820
(crowd claps)

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.070
- I was actually always into makeup.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:03.903
I loved it.

00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:04.990
I love seeing my mom
transform in the morning.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:07.350
I loved seeing her turn
into Superwoman, ya know?

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.098
Like I could see the
transformation in her.

00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:10.557
She felt more confident, she loved it,

00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:13.490
and I was like, "Oh my god
mom, this is like amazing."

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.740
And I loved it.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:15.573
- I love that.

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:18.820
Alright, did you struggle with
Manny's interest at first?

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.970
- I definitely did.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.602
Growing up in a latino household,

00:01:22.602 --> 00:01:27.331
the LGBT community
discussions never happened.

00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:29.810
It was something new to me,

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:34.236
so I had a real hard
time understanding it,

00:01:34.236 --> 00:01:35.772
and accepting it.

00:01:35.772 --> 00:01:37.933
- Cause you didn't grow up around it.

00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:38.766
- No I did not.

00:01:38.766 --> 00:01:39.703
- You grew up in a
completely different world.

00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:41.840
- Exactly. So it was very rough.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.010
- So Eva, beauty acceptance
is a big part of your brand.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.019
Do you relate to this?

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:47.170
- Oh completely.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.750
Especially what you were talking about,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.880
like my mother is my
biggest beauty inspiration.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.280
And those memories of watching her like,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.330
transform is a perfect word.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.920
She used to work at the
Hollywood Chinese Theatre,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.690
and back in the 80's I had
to go to work with her,

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:06.610
and she had to wear like the very Chinese,

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:07.580
I don't know what the proper word--

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.413
- [Kelly] The ensemble that
they wear, yeah yeah yeah

00:02:08.413 --> 00:02:11.240
- Is that gown, you know, with
the high collar and the red,

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.510
and I would watch her.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.710
We'd be on the bus.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.090
It would be super like not elegant,

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.440
except she would be this like, you know.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.273
- [Kelly] Beacon, yeah.

00:02:19.273 --> 00:02:21.430
- This thing and so that inspired me,

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.920
and continues to inspire me.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.482
That image of my mother
being this goddess, ya know.

00:02:25.482 --> 00:02:28.681
- I hope my daughter thinks I'm a goddess.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.670
(everyone laughs)

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.020
That's all I got from this.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.470
So I understand this got worse

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.710
as you got older though, right?

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.543
- Right.

00:02:36.543 --> 00:02:39.060
So as I got older, I
started to come into my own.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.890
And I was like you know, I love this,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.632
but I was scared that my
parents would not accept

00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:44.030
who I was.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:44.863
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:44.863 --> 00:02:45.696
- So I hid it from them.

00:02:45.696 --> 00:02:46.529
I hid it from them as I got older,

00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:49.100
and actually went to
counseling when I was little,

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.200
like a little counselor
moment just to be like,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.040
are you gay or not?

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.040
Let's make you not gay.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.150
And I'm like, "You got the wrong queen.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:56.983
It's not gonna happen."

00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:57.952
(crowd giggles)

00:02:57.952 --> 00:02:59.088
- You got the wrong queen!

00:02:59.088 --> 00:03:00.070
- Wrong one, you got the wrong girl!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.408
But it was very hard.

00:03:02.408 --> 00:03:06.202
It was a struggle for sure, but as I--

00:03:06.202 --> 00:03:07.613
- Well for someone to tell
you, especially as a kid

00:03:07.613 --> 00:03:09.570
no this isn't right.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.410
And you're like, wait well this is me,

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.930
why are you saying like I'm not right?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.000
What is, how do you change that?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:15.833
- You can't.

00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:16.666
You can't change it.

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:19.020
And so instead of changing,
I just like recluded.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.500
I was like, okay I'm
gonna live my whole world,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.820
my whole fantasy offline.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.850
I worked at Sephora inside JCPenny,

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.709
so I had my little JCPenny outfit.

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:26.580
- Yes

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.657
- I would get glammed for work,
so I would do this at work,

00:03:28.657 --> 00:03:29.780
but I didn't want my parents to see

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.080
cause I was so embarrassed.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.690
I was scared that they were
going to say something about it.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.350
I would glam at work, jump out my window,

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.730
go to work, come back and drive home,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.860
take off all my makeup before I got in,

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.355
and like walk in like, "Hey, wassup."

00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:43.260
- Alright, well how did
you finally come to terms,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.700
Manny senior, with your son?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.340
How did that finally evolve?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.270
- I think it was a big
turning point in my life

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:52.670
was when one day, it
was more of an argument,

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.500
more than a discussion with my wife.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.840
We had an argument, because
I was having a hard time,

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.673
she wasn't.

00:03:57.673 --> 00:03:59.650
She was a momma bear and
that's what she does.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.661
She was protecting her son.

00:04:00.661 --> 00:04:05.420
And she told me, and I remember
these words to this day,

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.851
is that, "If you don't find
a way to accept your son,

00:04:08.851 --> 00:04:10.635
you're gonna lose him forever."

00:04:10.635 --> 00:04:11.813
- Whew.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.877
- (choking up) And it
still, it still affects me.

00:04:16.877 --> 00:04:19.490
- You know why you're crying,
though, is because it matters,

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:20.340
and it's important.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.173
- It is.

00:04:21.173 --> 00:04:22.006
It definitely is.

00:04:22.006 --> 00:04:23.240
But there's still a lot of guilt there.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.630
- [Kelly] Yeah, you gotta forgive that.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.463
- Yeah.

00:04:26.463 --> 00:04:27.296
- Have you forgiven him?

00:04:27.296 --> 00:04:28.129
- [Manny] Absolutely.

00:04:28.129 --> 00:04:28.962
- He's forgiven you.

00:04:28.962 --> 00:04:29.795
Forget it.

00:04:29.795 --> 00:04:30.628
(crowd claps)

00:04:30.628 --> 00:04:31.461
Yeah!

00:04:31.461 --> 00:04:32.294
- Everyday, everyday.

00:04:32.294 --> 00:04:34.440
- You wanna know what,
you wanna know what?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.850
There are plenty of dads
out there that don't.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.070
And that's why I find
this story so important.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.167
Especially for this day and time,

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.344
right now what's happening in society.

00:04:42.344 --> 00:04:44.657
It's so important for you to say like,

00:04:44.657 --> 00:04:47.920
"Look, I didn't grow up around
this, and this is okay."

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.753
We have to change.

00:04:48.753 --> 00:04:50.770
We have to evolve, because
not everybody is the same.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.603
- [Manny Sr.] Absolutely

00:04:51.603 --> 00:04:53.010
- And it is very bold for
a grown man to get up,

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.460
that didn't grow up in that culture,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.790
to get up and wave that flag,

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.025
and say, "No, this is alright."

00:04:57.025 --> 00:05:00.442
(crowd claps and cheers)

00:05:02.238 --> 00:05:05.040
- And I'd like to also share
that it took me a long time

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:05.960
to get to where I'm at.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.882
It took me years and years.

00:05:07.882 --> 00:05:11.500
I went to counseling, and I
recommend that for anybody

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.830
that's struggling with
what I went through.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.663
- Yeah.

00:05:14.663 --> 00:05:16.880
- It's crucial that you get the help.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.170
- And because just at the same time

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.380
as you're going, "I can't change me,

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.360
I don't know how to change me."

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.133
He's going, "I can't change me.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.397
This is how I was built,
this is what I was taught."

00:05:25.397 --> 00:05:28.780
- And the thing is, it's
totally okay to not understand.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.680
What's not okay is not to try.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:31.513
You know, I think that's a

00:05:31.513 --> 00:05:32.980
really really big important message

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.610
is that it takes two to tango.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.700
I didn't try with him
because I was struggling.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.220
He didn't try with me
because he was struggling.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.170
And so we both just were clashing,

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.700
and it took some time for
us to get to the point

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.710
where it's like, I want to have
a relationship with my dad.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.170
He wanted to have a relationship with me.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.968
- Yeah, this is an incredible cool story.

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.189
- [Manny] Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:05:49.189 --> 00:05:50.022
(crowd claps)

00:05:50.022 --> 00:05:52.285
- Oh my gosh, like I love it.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.680
There is a happy ending to this.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.513
- Yeah there's a happy ending

00:05:54.513 --> 00:05:55.870
- There's a happy ending as well

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.181
because now you're all
business partners, right?

00:05:57.181 --> 00:05:58.014
- Yes.

00:05:58.014 --> 00:05:58.847
- And mom, right?

00:05:58.847 --> 00:05:59.900
- It's Grecka, right?

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.733
- Yes, Grecka.

00:06:00.733 --> 00:06:02.260
_ Okay, you're hiding. I
