Well Manny's story has
inspired countless families

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.610
including one from his
home town of San Diego.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:45.870
A 13 year old, Ernesto,
says Manny's videos

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.050
have made a huge impact on his life.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.650
He's here with his mother, Amber,

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:50.757
y'all come on out!

00:08:50.757 --> 00:08:53.340
(crowd cheers)

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.607
Hello, I'm Kelly!

00:08:58.646 --> 00:09:00.695
Nice to see you, come on out here.

00:09:00.695 --> 00:09:03.390
Ernesto, you look so handsome.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.919
My gosh, look at you in that mustard.

00:09:06.919 --> 00:09:09.583
- Hi! Oh my god it's
so good to see you too!

00:09:09.583 --> 00:09:10.520
- You look so handsome.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.442
Do y'all mind if we shift down a bit,

00:09:12.442 --> 00:09:13.586
and they can sit here.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:15.940
Here, Amber, Ernesto y'all sit here.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:19.090
We're shifting, it's like musical chairs.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.360
So you have something
you want to say to Manny?

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.780
- Yeah, I just wanted to say

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.570
that you're a really huge inspiration,

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.189
and I saw you at a meet and greet,

00:09:26.189 --> 00:09:29.070
and sadly I didn't have
enough time to tell you

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.620
how much you meant to me.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.726
But when I came out at 12,

00:09:32.726 --> 00:09:34.370
I always knew I was a little different,

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:37.420
because I was into
makeup and girly things.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.410
And I watched your videos to
help me feel better in my skin,

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.470
because I felt like
you made me feel better

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:44.773
that I could be a boy in makeup.

00:09:44.773 --> 00:09:46.089
Thank you.

00:09:46.089 --> 00:09:46.922
- Oh my god.

00:09:46.922 --> 00:09:49.422
(crowd claps)

00:09:52.544 --> 00:09:56.870
- I'm so, this is like why
I do what I do, ya know.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.710
It's getting to hear these stories,

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.870
and you know for me, I'm
just being myself online,

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.450
and I would have never
thought in a million years

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.990
I would have helped people.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.850
And hearing this it just
makes me feel so amazing

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:07.880
and that's why I do it.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:08.770
And I'm so proud of you.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.987
And your brows are snatched.

00:10:10.987 --> 00:10:12.730
How is this happening?

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:16.202
You look so good, I'm so proud of you.

00:10:16.202 --> 00:10:18.000
And for you to be out when you're 12,

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.790
it took me til, I wasn't
comfortable with myself

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.350
til I was 21.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.560
So it's just it's so awesome to see.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:24.440
I'm so proud of you.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.630
- I think what that means
though, as well Manny,

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.650
is we're progressing.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.450
We're progressing as a society

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.283
to where he feels comfortable.

00:10:31.283 --> 00:10:33.550
Just like yeah, I'm 12
years old and I'm gay.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.250
That's a really cool
thing that our society,

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.830
you feel comfortable
and you feel confident.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.580
Especially with this momma bear right here

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.860
who loves you either way.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.459
What does this story mean to you?

00:10:41.459 --> 00:10:45.320
- It was hard being a single mom,

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.020
and when I first had two boys, you know,

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:50.400
his older brother is rough and tumble,

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.960
when Junior came along it was different.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.450
We were always close and buddy buddy

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.210
so I thought maybe it's just a phase.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.200
Maybe it's because he's always with me.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.860
And then I kind of realized,
okay, this is here to stay.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.030
And I wasn't sure, do I embrace it?

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:04.880
What do I do?

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.730
I was, I wasn't scared that he was gay,

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:09.380
but I was scared how people
were gonna treat my baby.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.030
So Junior and I started
watching makeup videos together,

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:13.880
and he would help us.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.460
And he's like, "Hey mom,
here's Manny, look."

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.310
Manny is just Manny.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.460
Cause some people in
makeup, they are different,

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:21.300
or they're very feminine.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.147
But Manny is very Manny.

00:11:23.147 --> 00:11:25.009
(Manny laughs)

00:11:25.009 --> 00:11:26.097
Junior loved it

00:11:26.097 --> 00:11:29.070
and it was fun to watch
somebody that was like my baby.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.020
And it was okay.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:30.853
He's happy.

00:11:30.853 --> 00:11:31.686
He's successful.

00:11:31.686 --> 00:11:32.713
His family loves him.

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:36.790
So and then when Junior showed
me the video of Manny's dad

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:39.300
it helped me kind of
release a little stress,

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.240
because you feel kind of guilty, you know.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:45.113
What did I do, is this my
fault, did I do something wrong?

00:11:46.327 --> 00:11:48.200
And seeing Manny's dad

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.110
helped me just kind of
let some of that go,

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:53.380
because you're not sure how
people are gonna think or act

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.900
or what they're gonna do.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.530
And I felt maybe like I'm
not such a bad person.

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:58.720
I'm not a bad mom.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:01.480
Because I can instantly go,
"Oh my god, this is great."

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.380
I mean I was happy that
he was happy being him,

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.200
but I was still terrified.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.520
And seeing Manny's dad
love him through it,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.700
struggle through it, and get through it,

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.150
made me feel like, okay,
maybe I did the right thing.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:12.983
I can do this.

00:12:12.983 --> 00:12:15.015
(crowd claps)

00:12:15.015 --> 00:12:16.359
And be here for my baby

00:12:16.359 --> 00:12:18.400
- This is an amazing thing.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.240
I love it, I love it.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.390
- Can I just say, hats off to you.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.530
You have all my respect
as a single mother.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:26.447
That is the hardest thing ever.

00:12:26.447 --> 00:12:28.947
(crowd claps)

00:12:30.045 --> 00:12:31.480
- It's already hard enough as kids

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.330
and like who they're gonna be,

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.540
ya know what I'm saying?

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:34.530
It's hard to do all on your own.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:36.050
My momma did that as well for awhile,

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.010
so I applaud you as well.

